#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/ui/board-relocate.bpmn:79
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Before anything moves, name the content that would move — what it is, with its size and age — and where it lands. The confirmation sits in front of the move: an agent never relocates a durable artefact on its own initiative."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/ui/board-relocate.bpmn:63
#. Diagram label
msgid "Board renderer"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/ui/board-relocate.bpmn:44
#. Diagram label
msgid "Board: relocate content to the trashcan"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/ui/board-relocate.bpmn:90
#. Diagram label
msgid "Confirmed by the reader?"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/ui/board-relocate.bpmn:119
#. Diagram label
msgid "Drop its positions and sweep orphans"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/ui/board-relocate.bpmn:97
#. Diagram label
msgid "Leave the content exactly where it is"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/ui/board-relocate.bpmn:48
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Moving open content to the trashcan from the board, with the reader's confirmation in front of the move and not behind it. You are in this process when the fishbone is used on open content. The confirmation gateway has a real \"nothing moved\" end state, because a destructive action whose refusal is not drawn is a destructive action somebody performs by accident. The order of the two writes is the content of the diagram. The CONTENT relocates, and only then are its positions dropped and orphans swept — the folio carries what is true, the layout layer carries where it was drawn, and the arrow never runs the other way. Sweeping first would leave the board authoritative over the folio for the length of one step."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/ui/board-relocate.bpmn:78
#. Diagram label
msgid "Name what will move, and where it lands"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/ui/board-relocate.bpmn:145
#. Diagram label
msgid "no"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/ui/board-relocate.bpmn:104
#. Diagram label
msgid "Nothing moved"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/ui/board-relocate.bpmn:120
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Only after the content has moved: drop its positions from the layout layer and sweep any position whose note is now gone. Sweeping first would make the board authoritative over the folio for one step."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/ui/board-relocate.bpmn:58
#. Diagram label
msgid "Reader"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/ui/board-relocate.bpmn:109
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Relocate the confirmed content — that one thing, not the class it belongs to — to the trashcan. The folio changes first, because the folio carries what is true."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/ui/board-relocate.bpmn:108
#. Diagram label
msgid "Relocate the content to the trashcan"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/ui/board-relocate.bpmn:131
#. Diagram label
msgid "Say what moved and where it went"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/ui/board-relocate.bpmn:132
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Tell the reader what moved and where it went, so the content can be found in the trashcan rather than inferred missing from a card that disappeared."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/ui/board-relocate.bpmn:138
#. Diagram label
msgid "The content lives in the trashcan"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/ui/board-relocate.bpmn:74
#. Diagram label
msgid "The fishbone is used on open content"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/ui/board-relocate.bpmn:64
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The order of its five tasks is load-bearing: the folio move lands before the layer update, so an interruption between the two leaves the semantic content already relocated rather than the presentation layer half-updated against a folio it no longer matches. On \"no\", everything is left untouched."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/ui/board-relocate.bpmn:98
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The reader said no: nothing moves, no position is dropped, and the board is left exactly as it was. Drawn as its own end state because a destructive action whose refusal is not drawn gets performed by accident."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/ui/board-relocate.bpmn:91
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The reader's answer to A_AskConfirm, which named what will move and where it lands. `yes, move it` relocates the content to the trashcan; `no` leaves it exactly where it is. Nothing moves without the yes."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/ui/board-relocate.bpmn:144
#. Diagram label
msgid "yes, move it"
msgstr ""
